A||N||4||costly86gt||alternator problems?||||5||
Z||000000||costly86gt||04-16-2000||06:04 PM||||After I drive my car for awhile and put it in park, it dies on me.It will then start right back up.Also when I am at a stoplight with the blinker on the battery needle will move with the blinker.Every once in awhile it will just die after I start it.Could the alternator be dying?Basically everything on the car has been replaced except the alternator.||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-16-2000||06:09 PM||||Mine does the same thing.  I'm sure it's the alternator.  We've actually had a topic about this before.  Mine doesn't ever die on my though.  That might be something else...||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-16-2000||09:22 PM||||run a charging system check to make sure the alternator hasn't poped a diode. CHECK ALL the ground and battery cables VERY carefully. Especially the thin wires from the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Luperman||04-16-2000||11:59 PM||||It may not be the alternator mine was doing the same thing (dying after putting in park or just starting it ) until I inspected the IAC valve and found alot of carbon buildup not allowing it to open and close properly, as for the needle on the gauge moving when the turn signal is on that should be normal as long as the needle does dip below 12- 11 volts. good luck ||||reg||6
Z||000004||Luperman||04-17-2000||12:06 AM||||It may not be the alternator mine was doing the same thing (dying after putting in park or just starting it ) until I inspected the IAC valve and found alot of carbon buildup not allowing it to open and close properly, as for the needle on the gauge moving when the turn signal is on that should be normal as long as the needle does dip below 12- 11 volts. good luck ||||reg||6
